  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Along with its companion piece of the same size, The Second of May 1808 (or The Charge of the Mamelukes), it was commissioned by the provisional government of Spain at Goya's own suggestion shortly after the ousting of the French occupation and the restoration of King Ferdinand VII.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
